            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.138,
            0.901,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": "**Solution : Let us denote the number of pants by** x **and the number of skirts by** y. **Then the equations formed are :**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.451,
            0.183,
            0.898,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "y = 2 x - 2\\tag{1}",
          "image_source": "images/page_4_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.103,
            0.209,
            0.148,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": "**and**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.451,
            0.208,
            0.898,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "y = 4 x - 4\\tag{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_4_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.242,
            0.438,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "**Let us draw the graphs of Equations (1) and (2) by finding two solutions for each of the equations. They are given in Table 3.3.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.36,
            0.41,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "| x | 2 | 0 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| y = 2x - 2 | 2 | - 2 |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.236,
                0.331,
                0.34,
                0.349
              ],
              "content": "Table 3.3"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_table_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.449,
            0.41,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "| x | 0 | 1 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| y = 4x - 4 | - 4 | 0 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_table_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.247,
            0.898,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.629,
                0.536,
                0.715,
                0.556
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 3.2"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.572,
            0.9,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": "**Plot the points and draw the lines passing through them to represent the equations, as shown in Fig. 3.2.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.617,
            0.901,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": "**The two lines intersect at the point (1, 0). So,** x **= 1,** y **= 0 is the required solution of the pair of linear equations, i.e., the number of pants she purchased is 1 and she did not buy any skirt.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.692,
            0.901,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": "**Verify the answer by checking whether it satisfies the conditions of the given problem.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.753,
            0.587,
            0.772
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 3.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.783,
            0.901,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": "**1. Form the pair of linear equations in the following problems, and find their solutions graphically.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.824,
            0.902,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "**(i) 10 students of Class X took part in a Mathematics quiz. If the number of girls is 4 more than the number of boys, find the number of boys and girls who took part in the quiz.**"
        },
        {
